  All three mockups show the same page with a week picked (21–27 Sep). Only the event type control changes:

  - [1mA. Checkbox list[0m: all nine types visible at once, and you can tick any mix.
  - [1mB. Single Select[0m: everything on one row, one type at a time.
  - [1mC. Select with shortcuts[0m: B plus "Failed sign-ins" and "Security changes" choices.

  The labels and controls are wireframes. The real version will use the guideline tokens and components. I still
  recommend A, because one view can cover failed sign-ins and the security changes together.

  Have a look and tell me here which reads fastest. You can also click one in the browser.

